  "description": "Tests the Wenzl-Habiro keystone ansatz Q_β-Habiro(u) = W(u)·D(u) for the Q_β precision ladder. Each candidate W(u) (cyclotomic / Pochhammer-ratio surrogates for the level-2 SU(2) Wenzl annihilator at q = ζ_8) is Taylor-expanded at u = 0; the pair-specific D(u) is then determined coefficient-wise to reproduce the known c_k of the Q_β precision ladder. The structural acceptance test asks whether D(u) collapses to a clean closed form (small denominators, categorically-recognisable algebraic structure) or remains a generic Taylor series (which would be just refactoring without categorical content). Per AGENTS.md flip-flop history: numerical near-match ≠ structural derivation. This probe demands exact polynomial identity for c_2 = -1 first, then asks whether c_3 emerges naturally from the same Wenzl factor.",
